timestamp=2026-11-09T09:53:42.652Z level=INFO run=ce357dcf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# All readings become negative after offset. That means recorded values are all < 18000. \n# Is that plausible? Or is the offset direction/sign as stated? The rule says \"calibration_offset is defined as: (recorded value) - (true value)\". So true = recorded - offset. If offset is +18000, then true = recorded - 18000. If recorded readings are around e.g. 20000, true is ~2000. That gives positive true values. But if all recorded are small, true becomes negative -> dropped. That is correct per rules.\n# But let us look at actual recorded values for FARM_C in the window to understand scale.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
