timestamp=2026-11-09T09:54:55.659Z level=INFO run=ce357dcf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# FARM_G: recorded power values are mostly 0-409 kW. offset is +120. So true_power = recorded - 120. For many readings, recorded < 120 (e.g., 0, small), true_power becomes negative -> dropped. That eliminates most readings. Only when recorded > 120 do we get positive true_power. Is this the intended interpretation per the rules as written? Yes - \"Any value that is negative must be dropped, this rule is valid only after the calibration offset is applied.\" That is correct. So calibration offset can shift values below zero.\n# But let us also check the interval assumption. We assume 30-minute intervals (multiply power by 0.5 to get kWh). Is that correct? Looking at timestamps in the data - check frequency.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
