timestamp=2026-11-09T09:55:38.459Z level=INFO run=ce357dcf message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# 30-minute intervals. So factor 0.5 for kW -> kWh is correct.\n# Now look at another farm that gives 0, like FARM_E. Calibration says unit is BTU for FARM_E? Let us check: FARM_E has unit 'bTU' in calibration, and reading_type energy. Also value column meter_value. And offset is -50000.0. So true = recorded - (-50000.0) = recorded + 50000.0? Wait - calibration_offset is (recorded value) - (true value). So true = recorded - offset. If offset is -50000.0, true = recorded - (-50000.0) = recorded + 50000.0. That means true values are recorded plus 50000 - so true values become larger. That could be correct if sensors are under-reading? Let us look at actual recorded values.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
